PHP Branch Catch-Up Plan
Overview
The Python branch is significantly more advanced than the PHP branch. The PHP implementation currently has basic AI debugging functionality but lacks the sophisticated features developed in Python. This document outlines what needs to be built in PHP to achieve feature parity.

Current PHP Branch Status
Basic AI debugging script (ai-debugging.php)
Minimal LLM integration
No dashboard or MCP server
No iterative healing loops
No knowledge base or re-banker analysis
Required Features to Build
1. Core Healing System
Current: Basic single-pass debugging
Needed:

Implement iterative healing loop (similar to demo_full_healing_cycle.py)
Add temperature ramping (0.5 → 0.6 → 0.7) for multi-attempt fixes
Circuit breaker logic to prevent infinite loops
Error classification (syntax vs semantic vs logic)
2. Re-Banker Analysis Layer
Current: None
Needed:

Error parsing and classification system
Bug pattern detection (e.g., import errors, type mismatches)
Semantic analysis to provide LLM with contextual hints
Integration with healing loop to generate structured prompts
3. LLM Integration
Current: Basic API calls
Needed:

Support for multiple providers (OpenAI, LM Studio)
Proper async handling for long-running requests
Token management and cost tracking
Streaming response support
Error handling for timeouts and rate limits
4. Knowledge Base System
Current: None
Needed:

Success pattern storage (similar to envelope_storage.py)
Pattern retrieval for similar bug types
Confidence scoring and gold standard patterns
Database integration (SQLite or similar)
5. MCP Dashboard Server
Current: Partially implemented but not connected
Needed:

Complete MCP server setup (similar to dashboard_dev_server.py)
Real-time status updates
Knowledge base visualization
Healing session monitoring
CORS configuration for web access
6. Test Suite and Validation
Current: Basic tests
Needed:

Comprehensive test runners (similar to run_multi_attempt_test.py)
Bug complexity levels (simple, medium, extreme, nightmare)
Automated validation of fixes
Performance metrics and success rates
7. Configuration and Settings
Current: Hardcoded values
Needed:

Settings management (similar to llm_settings.py)
Environment-specific configurations
Model selection and parameter tuning
API key management
8. Error Handling and Logging
Current: Basic error output
Needed:

Structured logging system
Error categorization and reporting
Recovery mechanisms for failed healing attempts
Audit trails for debugging sessions
Implementation Priority
High Priority: Core healing loop and LLM integration
Medium Priority: Re-banker analysis and knowledge base
Low Priority: Dashboard UI and advanced features
Estimated Effort
Core healing system: 2-3 weeks
Re-banker layer: 1-2 weeks
LLM integration: 1 week
Knowledge base: 1 week
MCP dashboard: 2 weeks
Testing and validation: 1 week
Dependencies
PHP 8.1+ with async support
Composer for package management
Database (SQLite recommended)
Web server for MCP dashboard
